indielinks NEWS -- history of user-visible changes       -*- outline -*-

* 0.0.12

** User-visible changes

*** Increase the Activity Pub client timeout to 12 seconds
** Bugfixes

*** Use the query string when creating & validating Activity Pub signatures
* 0.0.11

** Bugfixes

*** Make sending `Create`s & `Reply`s more resilient

...by just logging failures to send intermediate results and moving
on, rather than failing the entire operation.
*** Make background tasks more resilient to failure

...by making the lease time configurable; a failing task should be
picked-up much less frequently, now.
** User-visible changes

*** Re-fetch the Actor on signature validation failure

I've been seeing failures to validate signatures from the
indieweb.social instance actor; when I fetch the actor manually, the
public key is different from what I had cached. This is an experiment
to see if I can catch rotated keys at runtime.
** Project updates

*** Bump the oldest-supported version of rustc to 1.96
* 0.0.10

** Bugfixes

*** Add support for the `Question` activity type
*** No longer fail a `/timeline` call because one outbox wouldn't parse
* 0.0.9

** Bugfixes

*** Stop polling the `tasks` table so much
** Operational changes

*** Return 413 Content Too Large on large payloads
*** Introduce `tracing_log_error`

When logging failures to fetch Outbox items, use a proper error reporter.
* 0.0.8

** User-visible changes

*** Allow unsigned GET ActivityPub requests
** Bug fixes

*** Stop spamming the logs on network outages

Stop returning openraft `NetworkError`s.
* 0.0.7

** Bug fixes

*** Get the bookmarklet working again
* 0.0.6

** Bug fixes

*** Fix the bookmarklet

It turns-out that "user" is a reserved word in DDB key condition
expressions, while not in ScyllaDB/Alternator.
** Project Updates

*** Bump ammonia in response to RUSTSEC-2026-0533
* 0.0.5

** Bug fixes

*** Always use the instance key to sign key requests
* 0.0.4

** Bug fixes

*** The documentation pages no longer 404 when reloaded
*** Fixed a deadlock when sending Follow requests
* 0.0.3

** User-visible Changes

*** Add docs to the front end

Add "about", user docs, terms of service & privacy policy.
** Project Updates

*** Make the front end customizable per instance
*** The Debian packages no-longer track indielinks.toml as a conffile

They now ship a configuration template which is rendered & intsalled in `postinst`.
* 0.0.2

** Bug Fixes

*** Rule out ActivityPub signature forgery
*** Fixed bug in how Notes are resolved from IDs

Cache ActivityPub Notes after resolving them, avoiding repeated HTTP
requests for the same remote Note.
*** Tighten-up XSS protection

Uniformly sanitize incoming HTML contained in AcitivtyPub messages.
** Project Updates

*** Added `cargo shear` to `run-linters`

Removed several unused dependencies in the doing.
*** Stop tagging frontend.asset.404s with the asset name

This produced a massive blow-up in the # of metrics being tracekd.
* 0.0.1

Initial indielinks release.

